1.What is Exception in Java?
An Exception is an unwanted or unexpected event that occurs during program execution and
disrupts normal flow of the program.
2.What is Exception Handling?
It is a mechanism to handle runtime errors so program does not crash.
3.Types of Exceptions
There are two type of exception in java
Compile time exception(Checked exception)
Run time exception(Unchecked Exception)

4.Checked vs Unchecked Exception?
1. Checked (Compile time exception): - these exceptions are checked at compile time by the java compiler.
Example: - 1.IO Exception.
2.SQL Exception
3.File not found exception
class Test {
        public static void main(String[] args)  throws Exception {
                            File Reader Fr = new File Reader(“text”. “text”);
     }
 }

2.Unchecked exception (Run time exception): - these exceptions occur during run program execution.
Example: - 1. Null Pointer Exception.
2.Athematic exception
3,Array index out of exception.
class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            int a = 10 / 0;
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Cannot divide by zero");
        }
    }
}

5.Difference between checked and unchecked
| Feature               | Checked           | Unchecked                   |
| Checked at      | Compile time   | Runtime                        |
| Handling           | Mandatory        | Optional                         |
| Example           | IO Exception    | NullPointerException |
6.What is try-catch block?
1.Try block: - the try block contains code that may cause exception.
If an exception occurs, the control immediately moves to the catch block
2.Catch Block: - The catch block handles the exception and prevents the programme from crashing.
try {
    String s = null;
    System.out.println(s.length());
} catch (NullPointerException e) {
    System.out.println("Null error");
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println("General error");
}

7.What is finally block?
The finally block always executes whether exception occurs or not.
8.What is throw and throws?
1.Throw: - throw used to create and thrown exception object.
2.Throws: - throws is used to declare an exception.
9.Difference between throw and throws?
throw	throws
1.Used inside the method body.	Used in method declaration
2.Used to throw a specific exception	                Used to declare exception
3.Throw one exception at a time	               Can declare exception multiple
4.Used with exception object	               Use with exception class name

10.What is stable element reference exception?
Stable element reference exception occurs when the referenced web element is no longer attached to dom.
It means selenium found the elemnt earlier but later the page is changed and that element reference become invalid.
Where does it ouccur
1.Page reload.
2.Page referesh.
3.Dom updated dynamically.
4.After ajax call,
•Solutions
1.Relocate the element
2.Use explicit wait
3.Use try catch.
11.What is no such element exception?
No such element exception occurs when selenium is unable to locate an element using the given locator within specified time.
When does it happen
1.Wrong locator
2.Element not presents in Dom
3.Page not fully loaded.
4.Frame not switched
5.Window not switched.
How to handle it
1.Use Explicit wait
2.Use find elements
12.What is element not interactable exception?
Element not interactable exception occurs when the element is present in Dom but not in a state that can be interacted with.
When it happens: -
1. Element is Hidden
2. Element is not visible
3. Element is disabled
13.	What is element click interactable exception?
Element click interactable exception occurs when another element is covering or blocking the target element when clicking
•When it happens: -
1.	Pop up overlay.
2.	Loader screen.
3.	Advertisement banner
